## 3. Exported galleries

Openhall does not claim ownership of exhibition-specific content generated for
a user. Subject to applicable law and the terms of any AI provider or other
third party involved, users may use, publish, modify, distribute, and
commercially exploit the exhibition-specific static gallery they generate and
export through Openhall.

To the extent an exported gallery contains portions of the Openhall Software,
the copyright owner grants the user a limited, non-exclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free permission to use, host, copy, and distribute those portions only
as incorporated into, and as necessary to operate, that exported gallery.

This export permission does not allow anyone to extract or reuse the Openhall
Software, source code, reusable viewer engine, templates, documentation, or
branding to redistribute Openhall, create a competing tool or service, or use
them independently of the user's exported gallery.

